 "notes": "3D modelling software cut from 72 to 7 archetypes (Blender, Maya, 3ds Max, Cinema 4D, ZBrush, Houdini, Rhino) plus 20 flat; dropped dead or niche (Softimage, trueSpace, Silo, Amapi, Aladdin4D, Animation:Master, VistaPro, E-on Vue, Electric Image, Hexagon, Realsoft, Art of Illusion, Anim8or and similar), trade/research (CityEngine, MASSIVE, Quake Army Knife) and non-3D-modelling tools (Oculus Medium, 3D Slash). CAD software cut from 59 to 7 archetypes plus 12; dropped trade, building-services and industrial CAD (FINE MEP, CATIA, NX, Creo, MicroStation, Tekla, Allplan, Cadwork, HiCAD, Caddie, Digital Project, BRL-CAD, KeyCreator, T-FLEX, SpaceClaim, Revit). Blender and Rhino stay on the 3D modelling kind. 3D printing slicer 18 to 2 archetypes plus 9 (dropped Skeinforge). New kinds Laser & CNC control software and Embroidery digitising software are sourced from reviews and a forum thread because no Wikipedia pages were found; LaserWeb, K40 Whisperer, Embrilliance editions and Ink/Stitch details were not on any retrieved page and are omitted. Circuit design 31 to 4 archetypes plus 12 (added EasyEDA and Fritzing from the retrieved comparison page; dropped industrial EDA: PSpice, SaberRD, ADS, Zuken CR/CADSTAR, PSIM, PowerEsim, Pulsonix, Micro-Cap, AutoCAD Electrical and similar). Photogrammetry 12 to 4 archetypes plus 5; dropped SOCET SET, IMAGINE Photogrammetry, Ames Stereo Pipeline (survey/defence/research), 3Dsurvey and dead Photosynth."
